-- title:
--   The injective factor of a compact operator is compact
-- statement:
--   Let $j:Z\to X$ be a compact operator between real normed spaces, and let $\tilde j:Z/\ker j\to X$ be the induced injective operator. Then
--   $$
--   \tilde j\ \text{is compact}.
--   $$
--
--   So compactness survives the passage to an injective operator, which is how the compact domain of the main construction is obtained.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/CompactQuotient.lean#L56-L69

